1
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:05,913
This is the hall of seals: every endorsed

2
00:00:05,913 --> 00:00:09,011
semantic model hangs here as its own medallion.

3
00:00:09,461 --> 00:00:13,200
Gold rings are Certified, slate rings are Promoted, and the

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,861
outer arc is how much of the year is left.

5
00:00:16,888 --> 00:00:19,698
Switch the lens to expiry and the hall

6
00:00:19,698 --> 00:00:23,618
regroups: expired, renewal due, valid, and no expiry.

7
00:00:24,419 --> 00:00:27,670
Today ranks what needs attention; this one flies me

8
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:30,729
to Sales Performance, ten days from running out.

9
00:00:31,532 --> 00:00:35,582
View as owner, and everything that is not mine steps back.

10
00:00:36,032 --> 00:00:37,072
Back to everyone.

11
00:00:39,685 --> 00:00:43,100
Open requests wait on the assay bench as unstamped

12
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:46,515
wax, with the reviewer’s progress around each one.

13
00:00:47,351 --> 00:00:50,486
On the assay desk, the owner’s claim and

14
00:00:50,486 --> 00:00:54,091
evidence sit beside my verdict for every item.

15
00:00:54,541 --> 00:00:57,699
Not applicable is only allowed for security,

16
00:00:57,699 --> 00:01:00,641
tests and labels, and only with evidence.

17
00:01:01,624 --> 00:01:06,224
Approving needs a note, and a Certified seal runs for twelve months.

18
00:01:06,674 --> 00:01:10,507
The app strikes the seal and records the review; I

19
00:01:10,507 --> 00:01:15,184
still apply the badge in Fabric, under Settings, Endorsement.

20
00:01:15,997 --> 00:01:19,807
Back in the hall, the new seal is pressed into

21
00:01:19,807 --> 00:01:23,782
the wax and hangs with the others, its arc full.

22
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:28,540
Renewals lists the seals whose arc is nearly drained.

23
00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:33,420
Start renewal opens a new request prefilled from the old one.

24
00:01:33,870 --> 00:01:37,770
The seal register holds the same records as a table, with

25
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:40,780
a trail check on every row and a CSV export.

26
00:01:41,594 --> 00:01:45,267
A checklist, a named reviewer and a trail you can

27
00:01:45,267 --> 00:01:49,014
show anyone: that is what a badge should stand on.
